-- title:
--   Affine chart at a supersingular point over the level field
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`; $q$ is a prime with $5 \le q$, $M'$ a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $A$ a valuation subring of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the non-units of $A$. Two function fields occur: `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-Laurent series generated by the coefficientwise images of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` $= \mathbb{Q}(\,$`qExpand ℚ d jq`$: d \mid M'\,)$, and `fieldBar q M'` $=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, the corresponding base change to $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ of the level-$(q^2M')$ field for the subgroup `levelH q M'` of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times}$, the kernel of the unit-group reduction `ZMod.unitsMap (dvd_sq_mul q M')`. The hypothesis `hle` asserts `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`.
--
--   Supersingular-place data: $W$ is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field of $A$, and `hW` says that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, that is, of the places $w$ which are rational (the structure map to the residue field of $w$ is surjective), are affine geometric places, and satisfy $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\,$`jGeomGen`$\,) \in$ `ssJSet q (ResidueField A)`; $s$ is an element of $W$.
--
--   Constant reduction: $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction A (modularFunctionFieldBar M') (modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M')`, i.e. a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` together with a surjective ring homomorphism `R₀.residue` onto `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ (a constant lies in `R₀.integers` exactly when it lies in $A$, and its residue is its image under the residue map of $A$), with a degree-preserving map on places matching orders of functions, and with the scaling property that every non-zero function can be scaled by a constant into `R₀.integers` with non-zero residue. The hypothesis `hR₀` says that $R_0$ computes coefficientwise reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image under `coeffMap A.subtype` lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over the residue field of $A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   Small constants: $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb{Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ has image in $A$; the hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` state that $A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \bar{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian local, and has algebraically closed residue field; `hκ` states that every $a \in A$ differs from some $c \in k_0 \cap A$ by an element of the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   Auxiliary prime and uniformisers: $\ell$ is a prime with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$; $\varpi_t \in k_0$ has image in $A$ and satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   Base layer: $K_b$ is an intermediate field of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with $K_b = \bot$, $A_b$ is a valuation subring of $K_b$ whose members are exactly the elements of $K_b$ lying in $A$, and $\varpi_b$ is a non-zero element of $A_b$ generating the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   With `fieldBar q M'` regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, the assertion is made for every intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ which is characterised by the stated coefficient condition: $f \in F_0$ if and only if for every $n \in \mathbb{Z}$ the $n$-th Laurent coefficient of $f$ lies in the image of $k_0$. For such an $F_0$ there exists a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ with the following eight properties.
--
--   (1) For $x \in k_0$, the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$ precisely when $x \in A$. (2) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring. (3) The image of $\pi_0$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (4) Lying over $s$: let $g$ be a Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$ belonging to `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, whose coefficientwise image in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in `R₀.integers`, and assume (i) for every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, if $P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of `jq` is non-negative then so is $P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of $g$, and (ii) the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$. Then the image of $g$ in `fieldBar q M'` under the inclusion given by `hle` lies in $F_0$, lies in $W_0$, and for every $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$ whose residue in the residue field of $A$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference between the image of $g$ and the image of $c$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (5) Level stability: for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$), every $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ lying in `Gamma0 M'`, and every $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` such that both $f$ and `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` lie in $F_0$, one lies in $W_0$ if and only if the other does.
--
--   (6) An affine chart: there exist a subring $B$ of `fieldBar q M'` and an $A_b$-algebra structure on $B$ such that the structure map sends $a \in A_b$ to the image of $a$ under $K_b \subseteq \bar{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`; $B$ is contained in the compositum (join) of the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_b$ and of $F_0$; every element of that compositum is of the form $g/h$ with $g, h \in B$ and $h \ne 0$; $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$; the quotient of $B$ by the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi_b$ satisfies `Ring.KrullDimLE 1`; every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$; the image of $\varpi_b$ in $B$ is prime; an element $f$ of $F_0$ lies in $W_0$ if and only if $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in B$ and the image of $\varpi_b$ not dividing $h$, so that $W_0$ is the localisation of $B$ at that prime; the image in `fieldBar q M'` of the class of `jq` lies in $B$; and $B$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` and every $\gamma \in$ `Gamma0 M'`.
--
--   (7) Finally, the special fibre of $B$ is identified with a Drinfeld quotient curve: for every algebra structure of `GaloisField q 2` on the residue field of $A$, every proof that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, and every $\zeta$ in `Idx q`, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the group of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of `GaloisField q 2` and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q (ResidueField A) Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the fixed field inside the Drinfeld function field of the subgroup generated by the actions of the elements of $C_s$) such that: the cardinality of $C_s$ equals $2\,\cdot\,$`placeWidthChar q M' s`, where the latter is `jWidthChar q` of $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(\,$`jGeomGen`$\,)$ divided by `placeRamificationJ M' s`; the kernel of $\rho$ is the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi_b$; on constants $\rho$ is reduction, namely $\rho$ of the image of $a \in A_b$ is the image of the residue of $a$ in the residue field of $A$; every element of the quotient field is a ratio $\rho(g)/\rho(h)$ with $g, h \in B$ and $\rho(h) \ne 0$; an element $z$ of the quotient field lies in the range of $\rho$ if and only if its image in the Drinfeld function field lies in the image of [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21); and $\rho$ is equivariant, in the sense that for $\gamma \in$ `Gamma0 M'` such that the pair (`redQ q γ`, $1$) lies in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) and for $f \in B$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹ f` also in $B$, the image of $\rho$ of the latter in the Drinfeld function field equals [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16) at that pair applied to the image of $\rho(f)$.
--
--   This is the construction, over the prescribed level field $F_0$ (the elements of the full level-$(q^2M')$ field all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients lie in the small-constants field $k_0$), of a discrete valuation ring $W_0$ lying over a chosen supersingular point $s$ together with an affine chart $B$ of the corresponding component of the semistable model, whose special fibre is the Drinfeld quotient curve with its $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/q)$-equivariance. It is obtained from [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_nodes_of_levelField`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_nodes_of_levelField) and feeds [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_affineChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_affineChart).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_of_levelField.lean

